Miriam Schmidberger: 15 Years of Leadership Coaching Partnership

Self-Awareness & Personal Foundation
Miriam helped me recognize my value as an individual — understanding that I have the right to stand up for my own interests, establish boundaries, and pursue my goals. This was foundational during my PhD years when academic pressure often blurs the line between dedication and self-sacrifice. She challenged me to build a clear sense of self before trying to lead others.

Emotional Regulation & Crisis Leadership
Especially in early career — during my PhD and high-pressure moments like the Scout24 major data incident — certain situations triggered panic in me. Miriam helped me calm down, step back from the emotional intensity, and then make clear decisions from a grounded place rather than reacting from fear. This capacity to regulate under pressure became essential as the stakes grew higher.

Understanding Childhood Patterns
She helped me see how my childhood was influencing my work and daily life — often in ways I couldn't recognize myself. We worked together to reflect on what happened in my early years, understand how those experiences shaped my reactions, and connect those patterns to my behavior in business contexts. As I resolved traumas and processed formative experiences, I became more conscious of my triggers and more deliberate in my responses. This deeper work fundamentally changed how I showed up as a leader.

Empathy & Active Listening
At Scout24, as I scaled from zero to 60 people, Miriam coached me to see others as complete humans with their own feelings, ambitions, and pressures. She moved me from passive hearing to genuine active listening — creating space for people to be understood holistically, not just through the lens of their deliverables.

Inner Clarity Before Leading Others
A recurring theme throughout Scout24 and Glomex: you cannot lead effectively while projecting unresolved issues onto your team. Miriam pushed me relentlessly to clean up my own "topics" first — unprocessed anxieties, unexamined biases, assumptions. Only with that inner clarity could I see my reports and peers for who they actually are, not distorted reflections of my own struggles.

Work-Life Balance & Intentionality
She challenged me to examine every activity: What is the actual value of this? This discipline helped me separate work from private life in a sustainable way, preventing burnout and ensuring I showed up fully present in both domains.

Authentic Communication & Public Speaking
For talks and presentations, Miriam coached me to find my authentic voice — clarity about what I actually believe and the courage to present my story without hiding behind jargon or borrowed frameworks.

Self-Trust & Team Trust
A critical insight: trusting yourself is the prerequisite for trusting your teams. Miriam helped me believe in my own decisions, which naturally cascaded into giving my teams real autonomy and ownership — the psychological safety that became a hallmark of my leadership at Scout24.

Navigating Conflict & Stakeholder Complexity
In difficult situations — friction with other leaders, competing priorities, organizational politics — she helped me step back, understand my own position clearly, map the other person's perspective with empathy, and find solutions that worked for everyone. This was essential for my C-suite and board-level stakeholder work.

Leadership Methodology & High-Performance Teams
We experimented with many leadership approaches and methodologies together, testing what actually transformed teams into high-performance units. This practical experimentation fed directly into the frameworks I later developed as a certified coach myself.

Cross-Cultural Leadership
Working with distributed teams — particularly my engineers in Kyiv — Miriam helped me understand cultural differences that shaped how people communicated, took feedback, and engaged with hierarchy. This wasn't surface-level awareness; it was learning to read what wasn't being said and adapting my leadership style accordingly.

Executive Communication
She challenged my conversations in all directions, especially upward. When I prepared for board meetings or executive discussions, she pushed me: Are you speaking their language, or are you being too theoretical? This sharpened my ability to translate complex technical concepts into business impact — a skill that became central to my C-suite advisory work.

Inspiring My Own Coaching Journey
Miriam motivated and supported me to go deeper — to not just receive coaching but to understand its foundations. She encouraged me to pursue my own coaching certification (Life Trust Coaching, 2022-2023), giving me a more holistic perspective on leadership development and the theoretical grounding to build my own frameworks for The Authentic Leader Academy.

Personal Support
Beyond professional coaching, as my wife she supported the demands of the role — the travel, the late nights, the mental load — making it possible for me to sustain high performance over years.